### 7.6 ChatService — The Orchestrator (Facade Pattern)

> This is the **most important class**. It glues everything together.

```java
public class ChatService {
    private final LLMProvider primaryProvider;
    private final LLMProvider fallbackProvider;
    private final List<Guardrail> inputGuardrails  = new ArrayList<>();
    private final List<Guardrail> outputGuardrails = new ArrayList<>();

    public ChatService(LLMProvider primary, LLMProvider fallback) {
        this.primaryProvider  = primary;
        this.fallbackProvider = fallback;
    }

    public void addInputGuardrail(Guardrail g)  { inputGuardrails.add(g); }
    public void addOutputGuardrail(Guardrail g) { outputGuardrails.add(g); }

    public Message chat(ChatSession session, String userText) {
        // Lock per session — prevents two messages in the SAME session
        // from corrupting the message list. Different sessions are NOT blocked.
        synchronized (session) {
            try {
                // ── Step 1: Run Input Guardrails ──
                Message userMsg = new Message(Role.USER, userText);
                for (Guardrail g : inputGuardrails) {
                    userMsg = g.validate(userMsg);
                }
                session.addMessage(userMsg);

                // ── Step 2: Compress history to fit token window ──
                List<Message> context = session.getOptimizedContext();

                // ── Step 3: Call LLM (with automatic fallback) ──
                Message llmResponse;
                try {
                    llmResponse = primaryProvider.call(context);
                } catch (Exception e) {
                    llmResponse = fallbackProvider.call(context);
                }

                // ── Step 4: Run Output Guardrails ──
                for (Guardrail g : outputGuardrails) {
                    llmResponse = g.validate(llmResponse);
                }
                session.addMessage(llmResponse);

                return llmResponse;

            } catch (GuardrailException e) {
                Message safe = new Message(Role.ASSISTANT,
                    "I cannot respond to this request due to safety guidelines.");
                session.addMessage(safe);
                return safe;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

