## 8. Design Patterns Summary

| Pattern | Where Used | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Strategy** | `LLMProvider` | Swap OpenAI ↔ Anthropic ↔ Gemini without changing `ChatService` |
| **Strategy** | `ContextManager` | Swap SlidingWindow ↔ Summarizer without changing `ChatSession` |
| **Chain of Responsibility** | `List<Guardrail>` | Add/remove/reorder safety checks independently |
| **Facade** | `ChatService` | Single entry point hides all internal orchestration |

---

## 9. Extensibility (SOLID)

| Principle | How it's applied |
|---|---|
| **Single Responsibility** | `ChatSession` manages state. `ContextManager` prunes history. `Guardrail` validates messages. `LLMProvider` handles network. Each class has ONE job. |
| **Open/Closed** | Want to add Gemini? Write `GeminiProvider implements LLMProvider`. Zero changes to `ChatService`. Want a new safety check? Write `NewGuardrail implements Guardrail`. Register it at startup. |
| **Dependency Inversion** | `ChatService` depends on interfaces (`LLMProvider`, `Guardrail`, `ContextManager`), not concrete classes. You can inject mocks for unit testing. |

