## 10. Important Interview Questions & Answers

### Q1: How do you handle streaming with output guardrails?
> **Problem**: You're streaming token-by-token. You can't check toxicity on individual words — "kill" could be part of "kill a process".
>
> **Answer**: Run input guardrails normally (before LLM call). For output:
> - Buffer tokens into sentences
> - Run toxicity check per sentence
> - If toxic content detected mid-stream, terminate stream immediately and return error
> - Optionally: run a fast async guardrail model in parallel

### Q2: What if the same user sends 2 messages in the same session simultaneously?
> **Problem**: Both threads read the same history, call LLM, and try to append to `ArrayList` → race condition.
>
> **Answer**: `synchronized(session)` in `ChatService.chat()`. This locks only THIS session. Other sessions run in parallel. Two messages in the same session are processed sequentially — which is the correct behavior for a chat.

### Q3: Multiple servers behind a load balancer — how do sessions work?
> **Problem**: User sends Message 1 → Server A. Message 2 → Server B. Server B has empty in-memory session.
>
> **Answer**:
> - **Option A**: Sticky sessions (load balancer routes same session to same server)
> - **Option B**: Centralized store (Redis) — all servers read/write from Redis
> - **Option C**: Hybrid — Redis as source of truth + local cache with TTL

### Q4: 10,000 active sessions, each with 500 messages — memory issue?
> **Answer**:
> - **LRU eviction**: Sessions idle >30 min are evicted from memory (`SessionManager.evictIdle()`)
> - **Lazy loading**: Don't load all 500 messages. Load only last 20 from DB. `ContextManager` only needs ~10.

### Q5: What if the primary LLM rate-limits you (HTTP 429)?
> **Answer**:
> - **Immediate**: Catch exception in `ChatService`, fall back to secondary provider
> - **Proactive**: Use a **Circuit Breaker** — if OpenAI fails 5 times in 60 seconds, stop calling it for 30 seconds and route all traffic to Anthropic
> - **Global**: Use a **Token Bucket Rate Limiter** shared across all sessions to stay under API limits

### Q6: How do you handle a chat history with 1 million messages?
> **Answer**:
> - **DB pagination**: Load only last 20 messages using `LIMIT 20 ORDER BY timestamp DESC`
> - **For older context**: Use **RAG** (Retrieval-Augmented Generation). Index old messages in a Vector DB. Search by semantic similarity to the current query. Inject relevant old messages as system context.
